abs/karate/commit/9ca3713f1d29a8399039f2866cc453cc024bf593","commit_subject":"karate-core: JWT auth, the Referer on a followed redirect, multipart parts as sent, raw request targets, and no invented Content-Type. configure auth { type: 'jwt', algorithm, secret | privateKey, payload, header, isSecretBase64Encoded, addTokenTo: header | query, headerPrefix, queryParamKey } signs with the JDK only (JwtAuthHandler): HS256/384/512 (Mac), RS* and PS* (RSASSA-PSS, MGF1 and salt matching the hash), ES* with the DER signature converted to JOSE r||s; the private key is PKCS#8 PEM; alg and typ are filled in as Postman does; Bearer and token are the defaults. A followed redirect carries Referer unless configure removeRefererHeaderOnRedirect. MultiPartBuilder keeps each part header's casing and adds no content-length or text/plain to a text part that names none. A request target may carry characters a URI rejects (braces, control characters), sent as given; a body with no Content-Type is sent without one rather than application/octet-stream. DESIGN says so. Failing first: JwtAuthHandlerTest (each family verified with the JDK, HS256 against RFC 7515's vector), MockE2eTest jwt, MultiPartBuilderTest 5/5, ApacheHttpClientRedirectRefererTest (unknown configure key), ApacheHttpClientRawTargetTest (Malformed escape pair), ApacheHttpClientNoContentTypeTest (application/octet-stream sent). karate-core 3020/0 (3 skipped).","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"growilabs/growi","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:46:54Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"a04e3916635992e22b5ce02f10950d3bf573e411","github_link":"https://github.com/growilabs/growi/commit/a04e3916635992e22b5ce02f10950d3bf573e411","commit_subject":"docs(model): create new indexes with migrations instead of Mongoose schemas","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"xorq-labs/xorq","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:46:39Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"0bb65b6eb058acba1598f31e0e7f45d700e38bbb","github_link":"https://github.com/xorq-labs/xorq/com